              "solutionId": "bfs-greedy",
              "solutionName": "Breadth First Search (Greedy)",
              "solutionDescription": "Use BFS/greedy approach treating the array as levels. For each level (jump), find the farthest reachable position from all indices in the current level. Move to the next level and increment jump count.",
              "timeComplexity": "O(n)",
              "timeComplexityExplanation": "We visit each index at most once while expanding the reachable range.",
              "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
              "spaceComplexityExplanation": "We only use a few variables to track pointers and counts.",
